**Room-creation rate limit (per uid).** `hostGame()` writes the room metadata and
a `hosts/$uid/lastCreated` throttle token in a single atomic update. The rules
reject that token â€” and therefore the whole room creation â€” when the same uid
created a room less than 15 s ago (`ROOM_CREATE_MIN_INTERVAL_MS` in `sync.js`,
mirrored by the `+ 15000` guard in `database.rules.json`). This caps how fast one
authenticated client can spin up rooms. Adjust both constants together if you
change the interval.
